Welcome to the Lisaac Ω world of CodEx !

For French teachers looking for a serious, fully functional, and entirely object-oriented language to
introduce a new approach to programming on solid foundations, Lisaac Ω is the ideal choice.

Lisaac Ω is a strongly typed language that supports design by contract. It is also a compiled language,
delivering the best performance across all platforms, even on smartphones.

In addition, Lisaac Ω offers a revolutionary feature: the possibility to write programs using graphical instructions,
making programming more intuitive and accessible than ever before.

One of Lisaac Ω’s major strengths is its seamless bridge between mathematics and programming.
Its syntax remains consistent with standard mathematical notations, and it includes fundamental mathematical
types with their traditional symbols, such as the type Z for integers.

Lisaac Ω is perfectly suited both for complete beginners discovering programming for the first time and for
experienced developers working on professional, highly portable software projects.
For advanced users, a wide range of graphical applications is available, along with the full source code of
the compiler (command 'lisaac') and the complete source code of the code editor (command 'elit').

In this repository, you will find a Lisaac Ω solution for the exercises available on:

https://codex.forge.apps.education.fr/parcours/

Lisaac Ω is free, entirely developed in France, and available on all platforms, including smartphones.
It represents a true revolution in programming languages.

Another unique advantage of Lisaac Ω is that it allows you, if you wish, to write code entirely in French,
making programming even more accessible to beginners and more natural in an educational context.

Choose a robust and innovative solution and give your students a solid foundation.

Make the switch to Lisaac Ω today!
